# Technical SEO — shared

One responsive URL (mobile-first index). Test **both** Lighthouse mobile + desktop.

## Crawl & index

- `robots.ts` + `sitemap.ts` + `pageMetadata({ path })` canonical on every page
- `noIndex`: 404, `?q=` on listings (canonical stays base path)
- `llms.txt` + AI crawler rules in `robots.ts` (English OK for llms)
- Server-rendered primary content; no orphan URLs; internal links between pillars

## Metadata

- Always `pageMetadata()` — title, description, OG/Twitter, `settings` for site defaults
- Articles: `publishedTime` / `modifiedTime` / authors when available
- One H1 per page matching visible title; metadata must match content (no bait)

## Structured data

- JSON-LD: `WebPageSchema` + type schema (`Article` / `Course` / `Service` / `ItemList`)
- `inLanguage: ur` · breadcrumbs via `BreadcrumbNav` on hierarchical pages
- Org / `SearchAction` in root layout — must match working search URL
- Schema must reflect visible UI (E-E-A-T → `07` / `.antigravityrules`)

## Performance hooks (device detail elsewhere)

- Images: explicit `sizes`; Sanity `.auto('format')`; lazy below fold
- Font: `DeferredUrduFont` · LCP: `optimize-lcp` skill
- Skip link `#main-content` in site layout (a11y + crawlable main)

